Short:    Sega Genesis/Mega Drive emulator for CaffeineOS/AmigaOS
Author:   Pedro Cotter
Uploader: Pedro Cotter
Type:     misc/emu
Version:  1.5
Requires: PiStorm/Emu68, CaffeineOS, CyberGraphX, 8MB+ RAM
Architecture: m68k-amigaos


GenesisPlusGX v1.5 for CaffeineOS/AmigaOS
==========================================

A Sega Genesis / Mega Drive emulator for PiStorm/Emu68 systems
running CaffeineOS or AmigaOS 3.x with CyberGraphX.

Based on Genesis Plus GX by Charles MacDonald / ekeeke.
Amiga port by Pedro Cotter.


Requirements
------------

- PiStorm with Emu68 JIT
- CaffeineOS or AmigaOS 3.x
- CyberGraphX (RTG)
- 8 MB RAM minimum (16 MB recommended)
- Chip RAM available for Paula audio buffers
- Optional, for GPU output: Pi 4 / CM4 and minigl.library 29.1
  (PiStorm3D). CaffeineOS already includes the library.


Installation
------------

1. Copy GenesisPlusGX anywhere on your hard drive
2. Run it from Shell/CLI with a ROM path
3. A default config file is created on first run


Usage
-----

  GenesisPlusGX <romfile> [options]

  Options:

    -14bit          Use 14-bit Paula stereo audio (4 channels)
    -ahi            Use AHI audio output
    -nosound        Disable audio
    -paulafreq=N    Paula/14bit sample rate (default: 44100)
    -ahifreq=N      AHI sample rate: 22050, 27710, 32000, 44100
    -scanlines=N    Scanline mode: 0=off, 1=25%, 2=50%, 3=75%
    -vsync=N        VSync: 0=off (default), 1=on (double-buffered)
    -frameskip=N    Frameskip: 0=off, 1=auto, 2=every 2nd, 3=every 3rd
    -fps=N          FPS counter: 0=off, 1=on
    -fmvol=N        FM preamp 10-100 (default: 85)
    -psgvol=N       PSG preamp 10-200 (default: 80)

  Examples:

    GenesisPlusGX roms/Sonic2.md
    GenesisPlusGX roms/OutRun.md -14bit -vsync=1 -fps=1
    GenesisPlusGX roms/SoR2.md -ahi -ahifreq=44100


Controls
--------

  D-Pad          Arrow keys / Joystick
  A              Z / Fire 1
  B              X / Fire 2
  C              C / Fire 3
  Start          Enter

  F5             Save state
  F8             Load state
  ESC            Quit


Configuration File
------------------

  PROGDIR:GenesisPlusGX.cfg

  Created automatically on first run. Edit with any text editor.

  ; audio: paula (8bit stereo), 14bit (14bit stereo), ahi, off
  audio=paula
  paulafreq=44100
  ahifreq=44100
  scanlines=2
  vsync=0
  frameskip=2
  fps=1
  fmvol=85
  psgvol=80
  paulafilter=0
  paulaboost=1
  paulastereo=1
  ahiboost=1

  Command line options override config file settings.
  Delete the config file to regenerate with defaults.


Audio Modes
-----------

  paula (default)
    8-bit stereo via audio.device. Two channels, lowest CPU cost.
    Good quality for most games. Uses paulaboost for volume.

  14bit
    14-bit stereo via audio.device. Four Paula channels:
    HI pair (volume 64) + LO pair (volume 1).
    Slightly better quality on clean PCM samples.
    Uses paulaboost for volume. ~2x audio CPU vs 8-bit.

  ahi
    16-bit stereo via AHI. Best quality, requires AHI drivers.
    Uses ahiboost for volume.

  paulaboost / ahiboost values:
    0 = 1x (quiet, no clipping)
    1 = 2x (default, good balance)
    2 = 4x (loud, may clip on loud games)


Video
-----

  Opens a CyberGraphX RTG screen in 16-bit color.
  BGRA pixel format is auto-detected and preferred.
  Double-buffered VSync available via vsync=1.

  Optional GPU output (glout=1 or -gl, Pi 4 / CM4 only) draws the
  picture through the V3D GPU with minigl.library 29.1: any screen
  size, scanlines and a composite blend. CaffeineOS already includes
  minigl.library; elsewhere install it from the PiStorm3D release.
  It looks better but is not faster (about 6 ms of CPU per frame).

  Scanline modes simulate CRT look:
    0 = off (sharp pixels)
    1 = 25% darkening
    2 = 50% darkening (recommended)
    3 = 75% darkening


Save States / SRAM
------------------

  F5 saves emulator state to PROGDIR:saves/<romname>.gsx
  F8 loads saved state.

  Battery-backed SRAM is auto-saved on exit and auto-loaded
  on startup to PROGDIR:saves/<romname>.srm


Supported Formats
-----------------

  .md  .bin  .smd  .gen  - Genesis/Mega Drive ROMs
  .gg                     - Game Gear ROMs
  .sms                    - Master System ROMs

  Max ROM size: 8 MB. Zipped ROMs are not supported.


Changes
-------

  v1.5 (19.02.2026)
  - Paula audio backend rewritten to be fully non-blocking
    WaitIO() replaced with CheckIO() poll across all slots
    Eliminates cascading buffer underruns on Pi 3 PiStorm
    Paula and Paula14 buffer count increased from 3 to 4
  - New lowcpu config option (lowcpu=1)
    Disables hq_fm and hq_psg, saving ~4ms/frame on Pi 3
    No audible difference on 8-bit Paula output
  - New -lowcpu command line flag
  - New 'make pi3' / 'build.bat pi3' convenience build target
    Compiles with all ASM optimisations for Pi 3 PiStorm

  v1.4 (18.02.2026)
  - 14-bit Paula audio rewritten using audio.device CMD_WRITE
  - 14-bit now uses same triple-buffered approach as 8-bit
  - Volume boost (paulaboost) support for 14-bit mode
  - BGRA pixel format auto-detection for VideoCore
  - FPS counter ghosting fix
  - Config file comments updated with audio mode descriptions

  v1.3 (17.02.2026)
  - BGRA mode selection for RTG screens
  - Fast RAM staging for Paula audio buffers
  - 14-bit Paula audio backend (initial)
  - FPS counter overlay

  v1.2
  - Configuration file support (GenesisPlusGX.cfg)
  - Scanline rendering modes
  - AHI audio backend
  - Double-buffered VSync

  v1.1
  - Save state support (F5/F8)
  - SRAM battery backup persistence
  - Stereo Paula audio
  - Volume boost options

  v1.0
  - Initial release
  - Genesis/Mega Drive, Game Gear, Master System
  - Paula 8-bit audio
  - CyberGraphX RTG video
  - Keyboard and joystick input


